  "sentences": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Microsoft just built a Surface laptop that can cost almost six thousand dollars.",
      "wordStart": 0,
      "wordEnd": 12,
      "start": 0.03,
      "end": 5.3
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "And somehow, the price isn't even the craziest part.",
      "wordStart": 13,
      "wordEnd": 21,
      "start": 5.3,
      "end": 9.665
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Microsoft teamed up with Nvidia to build the new Surface Laptop Ultra,",
      "wordStart": 22,
      "wordEnd": 33,
      "start": 9.665,
      "end": 14.18
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "powered by Nvidia's new RTX Spark chip.",
      "wordStart": 34,
      "wordEnd": 40,
      "start": 14.18,
      "end": 17.41
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "And this is very different from your normal laptop GPU.",
      "wordStart": 41,
      "wordEnd": 50,
      "start": 17.41,
      "end": 20.93
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Instead of having regular RAM over here, and separate graphics memory over there,",
      "wordStart": 51,
      "wordEnd": 63,
      "start": 20.93,
      "end": 25.82
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "the CPU and Nvidia GPU can share the same 128 pool of memory.",
      "wordStart": 64,
      "wordEnd": 76,
      "start": 25.82,
      "end": 28.74
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "gigabytes of it.",
      "wordStart": 77,
      "wordEnd": 79,
      "start": 28.74,
      "end": 29.785
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "Now, Microsoft that does not mean you're getting an Nvidia graphics card with 128 gigs of VRAM.",
      "wordStart": 80,
      "wordEnd": 96,
      "start": 29.785,
      "end": 34.95
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "The actual GPU is a Blackwell RTX GPU, with up to 6,144 CUDA cores.",
      "wordStart": 97,
      "wordEnd": 110,
      "start": 34.95,
      "end": 40.095
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "But because it can access that huge shared memory pool,",
      "wordStart": 111,
      "wordEnd": 120,
      "start": 40.095,
      "end": 43.175
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "it can handle workloads that normally wouldn't even fit into a laptop GPU's memory.",
      "wordStart": 121,
      "wordEnd": 134,
      "start": 43.175,
      "end": 47.795
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "And that's where things get ridiculous.",
      "wordStart": 135,
      "wordEnd": 140,
      "start": 47.795,
      "end": 49.98
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "Nvidia says RTX Spark delivers up to one petaflop of AI inference performance.",
      "wordStart": 141,
      "wordEnd": 153,
      "start": 49.98,
      "end": 54.735
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "That's about five times faster than the previous generation.",
      "wordStart": 154,
      "wordEnd": 162,
      "start": 54.735,
      "end": 57.32
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "So if you're a developer .",
      "wordStart": 163,
      "wordEnd": 168,
      "start": 57.32,
      "end": 58.3
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "text": "building and running NVIDIA complex says AI models RTX Spark",
      "wordStart": 169,
      "wordEnd": 178,
      "start": 58.3,
      "end": 61.62
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "text": "delivers up to one petaflop of AI performance, and can",
      "wordStart": 179,
      "wordEnd": 188,
      "start": 61.62,
      "end": 67.035
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "text": "run AI models with around 120 billion parameters locally, as in on your laptop.",
      "wordStart": 189,
      "wordEnd": 202,
      "start": 67.035,
      "end": 77.765
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "No giant desktop workstation, no sending the entire model to the cloud.",
      "wordStart": 203,
      "wordEnd": 214,
      "start": 77.765,
      "end": 85.88
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "text": "And Microsoft didn't exactly HDMI, put USBA all of this and USBC,",
      "wordStart": 215,
      "wordEnd": 226,
      "start": 85.88,
      "end": 91.97
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "text": "all in a laptop weighing under 4.5 pounds.",
      "wordStart": 227,
      "wordEnd": 234,
      "start": 91.97,
      "end": 95.82
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "text": "They even made the USBC charger magnetic.",
      "wordStart": 235,
      "wordEnd": 241,
      "start": 95.82,
      "end": 99.395
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "text": "But then, there's the price.",
      "wordStart": 242,
      "wordEnd": 246,
      "start": 99.395,
      "end": 102.015
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "text": "The Surface Laptop Ultra starts at $2,599.",
      "wordStart": 247,
      "wordEnd": 253,
      "start": 102.015,
      "end": 107.275
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "text": "And if you want that ridiculous 128 gigabyte configuration, you're looking at $5,899.99.",
      "wordStart": 254,
      "wordEnd": 266,
      "start": 107.275,
      "end": 116.725
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "text": "So, yeah.",
      "wordStart": 267,
      "wordEnd": 268,
      "start": 116.725,
      "end": 117.955
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "text": "that Microsoft basically basically built a built portable a Nvidia",
      "wordStart": 269,
      "wordEnd": 278,
      "start": 117.955,
      "end": 120.06
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "text": "portable AI workstation and disguised it as a surface laptop.",
      "wordStart": 279,
      "wordEnd": 288,
      "start": 120.06,
      "end": 124.79
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "text": "The only question is, who actually needs this much laptop?",
      "wordStart": 289,
      "wordEnd": 298,
      "start": 124.79,
      "end": 131.6
    }
  ],
